32-bit assembly code:
- Use open() syscall:
  - %eax hold syscall number 5.
  - %ebx hold address of the first character of filename (array of characters).
  - %ecx hold read/write operation for the file.
  - %edx hold permission for the file.
- After using open() syscall, linux kernel return file descriptor in %eax.
- Use read() syscall (number 3):
  - %ebx hold file descriptor.
  - %ecx hold address of buffer for storing data that is read.
  - %edx hold the size of the buffer.
  - %eax hold number of characters read or error code.
- Use write() syscall (number 4):
  - %ebx hold file descriptor.
  - %ecx hold address of buffer filled with data to write.
  - %edx hold the size of the buffer.
  - %eax hold number of characters written or error code.
- Use close() syscall (number 6):
  - %ebx hold file descriptor.
